Subject: [PATCH] Drop the azure-bdist-wheel option from setup.cfg

setup.cfg sets `azure-namespace-package`, an option consumed by Microsoft's
azure-bdist-wheel setuptools plugin. That plugin is long dead and is not on
conda-forge, and current setuptools treats the unknown option as an error:

  error: error in setup.cfg: command 'bdist_wheel' has no such option
  'azure_namespace_package'

The package installs fine without it.

--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -1,6 +1,5 @@
 [bdist_wheel]
 universal = 1
-azure-namespace-package = azure-nspkg
 
 [egg_info]
 tag_build = 
